# Browser-verify UI changes

After any change that affects rendered UI (primitives, CSS tokens, sandbox samples),
**do not** report done until you have verified it yourself in a real browser.

## Required loop

1. Ensure the relevant dev server is running (sandbox / consumer app).
2. Use **cursor-ide-browser** (preferred) and/or Playwright when available:
   navigate → lock → snapshot → interact (click/type) → **screenshot** → unlock.
3. For visual bugs (gaps, alignment, continuous strips, hover/focus), take an
   element or viewport screenshot and inspect it — do not rely on CSS reasoning alone.
4. When geometry matters, also use CDP `Runtime.evaluate` / bounding boxes to
   confirm continuity (e.g. adjacent range bars abut with no gap).
5. If verification fails, fix and re-verify in the same turn.

## Scope

Applies to UI work in this repo. Skip only for pure non-visual tasks (types-only,
docs-only with no visual claim, git/PR plumbing).
